            "It sounds like you're referring to Rodin's sculpture titled \"The Fallen Caryatid Carrying Her Stone.\" This sculpture is part of Rodin's series inspired by the caryatids, which are architectural supports often in the form of female figures. In this work, he portrays a woman stooped and struggling under the weight of a stone, symbolizing the burden of life. It's a powerful and emotive piece. Is there anything specific you'd like to know about it?"
          ]
